Hi all,

This is just a short message to tell you all that the patches for
NetHack: the Next Generation are now available by ftp. To get them,
type the following:

	ftp ftp.krl.caltech.edu
	(usercode) anonymous
	(password) your own usercode	(not your password)
	cd /pub/nethack/NhTNG
	hash				(optional)
	binary				(NOT optional)
        get README
	get nh313.tng.shar
	quit

This will copy the files README and nh313.tng.shar to your own system.
The second of these files contains new files for the source code plus
some patches to perform some changes to your original NetHack
distribution. Note that these patches are NOT official and NOT
sanctioned by the Dev Team. Read the disclaimer in the README file
before doing anything else.

If you have no access to the ftp protocol, but you HAVE e-mail (which
you usually have if you can read the news), than you might want to try
the ftpmail server: send . Make a message that just says "help", and
send it to ftpmail@decwrl.dec.com, and you'll be sent a file that tells
you how to get ftp-available files via mail.

Boudewijn Wayers, krl ftp site manager. If you have anything to
contribute, let me know...

